// P-PACK Phase 3 + P-NUM-SYM: assignment between numeric types is strict. A `float` literal does not
// silently narrow to `f32`, nor does `f32` widen to `float`. `f32` is a strict fixed-width type, so
// neither assignment nor arithmetic widens it. Construct an `f32` with the `f32` suffix instead.
// expect: error E0007 at 7:14
// expect: error E0007 at 8:16
// expect: exit 1
mut a: f32 = 1.0
mut b: float = 1.0f32
echo a
echo b
